  "verbalization": "Levomilnacipran is shown to interact with Cyp2j2 through binding, which in turn participates in multiple metabolic activities, including arachidonic acid monooxygenase and epoxygenase activities, and aromatase activity. These activities are all performed by Cyp2c8, suggesting a potential link between Levomilnacipran and Cyp2c8 through a shared pathway involving Cyp2j2. The evidence indicates that Levomilnacipran may influence Cyp2c8 via Cyp2j2, possibly through a mechanism where the drug modulates the activity of Cyp2j2, which then indirectly affects Cyp2c8. The overlapping participation of Cyp2j2 in different metabolic processes supports the idea that Levomilnacipran could exert its effects on Cyp2c8 through a complex, multi-step interaction involving Cyp2j2. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
